Cell["\<\
Hypothesis: 
- When food reward is low, cost of false alarming is too much that best case \
is to not lick, i.e. decision threshold extremely high. 
- When food reward is medium, you start licking, and paying more attention. \
Decision threshold decreases. We see some case where d prime increases only, \
and some cases where d prime increases and then decreases. The latter case \
would be when after some point increasing d prime becomes more \
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.908985918371891*^9, 3.908985927486905*^9}, {
   3.90898791060822*^9, 3.908988066298911*^9}, 
   3.9089881962119303`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"dbc50e4b-8c8a-4b29-81d4-\
4e038bee0330"],

